# `lines(source: Trimmed)`: the shortcut's `Trimmed.read` names the `read` it hands on to, `Source.read(self)`, a
# call through a class: it runs that method and nothing in its place, on the source it is handed first, so a trimmed
# source that is a feed never reads its store and the route asks the network alone. What `read` gives is bytes, no
# type of the code's: it goes back to the call that ran it.

route news.read.lines
step lines/Trimmed.read
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read                                                    # `Source.read(self)`
step lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen

line entry > lines call
line Trimmed·source > lines value
line Trimmed·source > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen value         # `urlopen(self.url)`
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen > _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen value
line _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read value   # `response.read()`
line Web > lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read own                                         # `urlopen(self.url)` with no data is a GET
line lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read > lines/Trimmed.read back
line lines/Trimmed.read > lines back

# the source `Source.read` is handed rests at its own arrow, and `urlopen` takes the signature's type from beyond

home Trimmed·source lines
home _·response@lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read/urlopen lines/Trimmed.read/Source.read

side entry left
side Web left                                                                         # `urlopen(url)` with no data is a GET

# `cached_lines(source: Cached)`: the call is `Cached.read` or, on a feed, `Trimmed.read` on the feed, drawn as
# `Feed.read` (#155). The shortcut's `Trimmed.read` names `Source.read(self)`, so on a feed the call asks the network
# and never reads the store: a cached source that is also trimmed is no cache. On any other cached source the store is
# read, else the network and then the store.

route news.read.cached_lines
step cached_lines/Cached.read one of 2                                            # `source.read()`, one of two
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Store.has
choice cached_lines/Cached.read/?1
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.get
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read                                      # `super().read()`
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen
step cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.put
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read                                           # what it runs on a feed
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read                               # `Source.read(self)`
step cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read/urlopen

line entry > cached_lines call
line Cached·source > cached_lines value
line cached_lines/Cached.read > cached_lines back

# on any cached source: the store, else the network and then the store
line Cached·source > cached_lines/Cached.read/Store.has value                    # `self.store.has(self.url)`
line cached_lines/Cached.read/Store.has > cached_lines/Cached.read back
line Cached·source > cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.get value
line Disk(self.root / key) > cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.get own
line cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.get > cached_lines/Cached.read back
line Cached·source > cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen value       # `urlopen(self.url)`
line cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen > _·response@cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen value
line _·response@cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen > cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read value   # `response.read()`
line Web > cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read own
line cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read > _·data@cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read value
line _·data@cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read > cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.put value
line Cached·source > cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.put value
line cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Store.put > Disk(self.root / key) own
line _·data@cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read > cached_lines/Cached.read value   # `return data`

# on a feed: the network alone
line cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read > cached_lines/Cached.read back
line cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read > cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read back
line Cached·source > cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read/urlopen value
line cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read/urlopen > _·response@cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read/urlopen value
line _·response@cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read/urlopen > cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read value
line Web > cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read own


home Cached·source cached_lines
home _·response@cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read/urlopen cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read
home _·data@cached_lines/Cached.read/?1/Source.read cached_lines/Cached.read
home _·response@cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read/urlopen cached_lines/Cached.read/Feed.read/Source.read

side entry left
side Web left                                                                         # `urlopen(url)` with no data is a GET
side Disk(self.root / key) both
